  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "039c4401-b78e-46c5-96f5-c3cbc73a3bb8",
      "name": "Note - Overview & Setup Checklist",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        256,
        -304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1144,
        "content": "## 🎬 Slack Chat-to-Avatar-Video Bot\n\n### How it works\n\nMessage a news headline to your Slack bot → an AI Agent drafts a 30-second English broadcast script → you approve or ask for edits right in the Slack thread → once you confirm, HeyGen generates a talking-avatar video → the bot replies with the video link. Each conversation's state (draft script, status, HeyGen job ID) lives in an n8n Data Table, since two Slack messages are two independent events with no shared memory otherwise.\n\n### Setup checklist (do these before testing)\n\n**1. Create your Slack app** (api.slack.com/apps → Create New App → From scratch):\n- OAuth & Permissions → Bot Token Scopes: `chat:write`, `channels:history`, `im:history`, `users:read`\n- Event Subscriptions → turn on, set the Request URL to this workflow's \"When Slack Message Received\" node production webhook URL (shown once you activate the workflow), subscribe to bot events `message.channels` and `message.im`\n- Install the app to your workspace, then invite the bot into the channel (or DM it)\n- Copy the Bot User OAuth Token + Signing Secret into a new Slack credential in n8n, and connect it to every Slack node here (the trigger and all \"Post/Notify ... to Slack\" nodes)\n\n**2. Create a Data Table** (e.g. `slack_video_sessions`) with columns: `channelId`, `newsContent`, `script`, `status`, `heygenVideoId` — all string type. Point every Data Table node at it.\n\n**3. HeyGen**: create a Header Auth credential (Header Name: `X-Api-Key`, value = your HeyGen API key) and connect it to \"Create HeyGen Video\" and \"Verify HeyGen Video Status\". Replace `avatar_id`/`voice_id` in \"Create HeyGen Video\" with your own (HeyGen → Avatars / Voices — these are two separate IDs even for the same avatar).\n\n**4. OpenAI**: connect your own OpenAI credential to both model nodes (\"Generate Script with OpenAI\", \"Revise Script with OpenAI\").\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the AI prompts for script tone/length, the Slack confirmation keywords in \"Check User Confirmation\", the HeyGen avatar/voice/resolution settings, and the 15s/20-try polling limit to fit your needs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9753326d-be7b-4ff2-bcc6-b763b8e5715e",
      "name": "Note - Receive & Validate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        976,
        688
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "## Receive & validate the message\n\nListens for Slack message events and parses the payload into channelId/userId/text/isBot/subtype. Anything with no text, or sent by the bot itself (its own replies, message edits), is dropped here instead of being treated as a new request — otherwise the bot would reply to itself in a loop."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f050226f-a2d6-454a-9cd1-41477aacfafe",
      "name": "Note - Session Lookup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1808,
        688
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "## Find pending session\n\nQueries the Data Table for a session on this channel with status = awaiting_confirmation. Found → this message is a reply (confirm/feedback) to an existing draft. Not found → it's a brand-new news request."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "96daa04b-7bbb-4987-aeb4-5e7fac2bd14a",
      "name": "Note - Generate New Draft",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2336,
        1408
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## Generate a new draft\n\nAn AI Agent (backed by OpenAI) turns the news content into a 75-85 word English broadcast script (~30 seconds of read time, no title/markdown), saves it to the Data Table as awaiting_confirmation, and posts it to Slack asking the user to confirm or ask for changes. The error-output branch tells the user in Slack if this step itself fails."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "34cebef5-cb1f-4b79-b3be-4a380987f7d4",
      "name": "Note - Confirm or Revise",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2336,
        320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## Confirm or revise\n\nRegex-matches the reply against approval words (confirm/continue/approved/yes/ok...). Match → mark the session confirmed and start the HeyGen video job. No match → a second AI Agent rewrites the script using the stored draft plus the feedback, and posts the revision back to Slack for another round — loop through as many revisions as needed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "24576745-9569-49e3-80ba-17beda9d0021",
      "name": "Note - Start HeyGen Job & Poll",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3248,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1220,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Start the HeyGen job & poll\n\nPOSTs the confirmed script to HeyGen's /v3/videos endpoint — an async render job, not an immediate result. If the call itself fails, Slack is notified right away. Otherwise the job ID is saved and a Loop Over Items node (reset mode) checks status every 15 seconds, for up to 20 tries (~5 minutes) before giving up as timed out."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b3b4e09a-6e38-4f1e-9f0d-e6e7043d7d07",
      "name": "Note - Deliver the Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4576,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Deliver the result\n\n\"completed\" → the video_url is posted back to Slack and the session is marked completed. \"failed\" or 20 polls reached → a friendly apology is posted instead and the session is marked failed — the user can just message the bot again to start over."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
